<h1 class="hero-h">2026 Portable Fitness Ad Creative Benchmark: <em>19 live ads, measured frame by frame.</em></h1>
<p class="hero-sub">Most creative advice is opinion. This is measurement. We pulled 19 live Meta ads from TRX Training, Gorilla Bow and MAXPRO, downloaded the actual video files, and measured duration, aspect ratio, cut rate, average shot length, caption coverage and creative age. Then we audited the four storefronts those ads point at. No vendor sponsorship, no client data, every number reproducible from public sources.</p>
<div class="exec-summary"><div class="exec-l">Executive summary</div><p class="exec-p">Two editing rhythms dominate this category and almost nothing sits between them: brand-produced product films cut every 1.9 to 2.2 seconds, creator-fronted ads every 4.6 to 4.9. Caption discipline separates the leader from everyone else, with one advertiser captioning 100% of runtime and three ads carrying no on-screen text at all. Hook selection is heavily concentrated, with offer-led-with-a-number and contrarian-claim accounting for 14 of 26 mapped openings while pattern interrupt is used exactly once. On the funnel side the gap is proof: the category leader shows 908 reviews on its main product page, the nearest challenger shows five, and one advertiser has a review widget installed that renders nothing at all while its 842-day-old ad claims 100,000 happy customers.</p></div>
</div></div>

